== Rotation group of the regular tetrahedron
ok   all 24 vertex permutations are isometries of the regular tetrahedron
ok   12 of them are proper rotations (det +1), identity included
ok   proper rotations are exactly the even vertex permutations
     rotation angles (deg: count): {0: 1, 120: 8, 180: 3}
ok   types: identity 1, 120/240-degree vertex-axis turns 8, 180-degree edge-axis turns 3
ok   120-degree turns fix one vertex (vertex axis); half-turns fix none (edge-midpoint axis)
ok   4 destinations for one vertex x 3 placements of the rest = 12
ok   24 four-letter labellings fall into 2 rotation classes of 12 (4-5 P6 answer 2)
ok   a reflection carries one class to the other
ok   no non-identity rotation fixes a four-distinct-letter labelling (orbit size 12)
ok   all 12 A,A,B,C labellings are one rotation class (K-1 P4 / 2-3 P5 answer: no unmatched pair)
ok   all AABB labellings form one class too
ok   all AAAB labellings form one class too
ok   all AAAA labellings form one class too

