== Exhaustive testing as a proof (guide p1 "A finite list of unsuccessful turns alone is not an impossibility proof")
ok   once A is aligned only 3 rotations remain (identity and the two turns about A); all 3 fail on the mirror pair, so trying those three turns is a complete impossibility proof
ok   equivalently, all 12 rotations fail: an exhaustive finite list does prove impossibility

